## Why This Is Asked
This question validates the ability to design an automated security response system for multi-tenant Azure SaaS environments, integrating threat detection with immediate containment and recovery capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- Anomaly detection using Defender for Cloud analytics and Sentinel ML models
- Event Grid-based alert routing and per-tenant processing
- Automated resource isolation via NSG rules, private endpoint restrictions, and conditional access policies
- Key Vault credential rotation and token revocation workflows
- Deployment slot rollback with feature flag coordination
- Comprehensive audit trails across all security actions

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-logic for automated breach response
async function handleSecurityAlert(alert) {
  if (alert.severity > 3) {
    await isolateTenantResources(alert.tenantId);
    await rotateCompromisedCredentials(alert.tenantId);
    await initiateSafeRollback(alert.tenantId);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of Azure Policy and how to implement guardrails that cover new and existing resources, plus rollout and rollback planning.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Policy and Initiatives
- Deny vs DeployIfNotExists vs AuditIfNotExists
- Storage Account security controls (public access, HTTPS, encryption)
- Tag-based governance and rollout strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
{
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "allOf": [
        { "field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts" },
        { "field": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/publicAccess", "notEquals": "None" },
        { "field": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts.enableHttpsTrafficOnly", "notEquals": true },
        { "field": "tags.env", "exists": false }
      ]
    },
    "then": { "effect": "deny" }
  },
  "parameters": {}
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle existing storage accounts that violate these rules during rollout?
- What metrics and alerts would you configure to monitor policy compliance over time?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-service, tenant-aware, tamper-resistant logging with strict retention and quick rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Tamper-evident logging; per-tenant key management; HMAC; Key Vault rotation
- Multi-service sinks; Log Analytics and ADLS Gen2 immutable storage
- Real-time integrity checks; Event Hubs; Canary rollout; incident response

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: sign and write log
function signAndWrite(log, tenantId){
  const key = getKeyFromKV(tenantId);
  const signature = hmacSHA256(log, key);
  writeToSink({log, signature, tenantId});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify integrity without exposing keys?
- How would you handle key compromise and replay attacks?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to design identity guardrails across multi-tenant environments, integrating PIM, token hygiene, UEBA detection, and automated rollback capabilities. It reflects real-world risks associated with cross-tenant service principals in enterprise Azure deployments.

## Key Concepts
- Just-In-Time access via Azure AD Privileged Identity Management
- MFA enforcement on service principals
- Token hygiene and refresh token controls
- UEBA-driven threat detection and automated containment
- Defender for Cloud and Log Analytics integration
- Rollout planning and rollback criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
// Guardrail configuration pseudocode
const guardrail = {
  pim: {
    mode: 'JIT',
    autoRevoke: true,
    maxActivationMinutes: 240
  },
  mfa: {
    requiredForServicePrincipals: true,
    blockNonMfaRefreshTokens: true
  },
  ueba: {
    enabled: true,
    autoQuarantine: true,
    anomalyThreshold: 0.85
  },
  rollback: {
    targetState: 'last-known-good',
    autoRestore: true
  },
  monitoring: {
    defenderForCloud: true,
    logAnalytics: true
  }
};

// Rollout steps
async function rollout() {
  await configurePim(guardrail.pim);
  await enforceMfaPolicy(guardrail.mfa);
  await enableUeba(guardrail.ueba);
  await setupMonitoring(guardrail.monitoring);
  await testRollback();
}

// Rollback criteria
const rollbackCriteria = {
  jitterrorRate: 0.05,
  mfaFailureRate: 0.10,
 uebaFalsePositives: 0.20
};
```
